From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: a Linux program's button minimizes it when it is in front

David 2026-10-03: a program in front, its taskbar button clicked, did not
minimize. Windows programs did; a Linux program in its frame (0762) did
not: a click on the taskbar takes the X focus from the program's window
inside its frame for a moment, so Wine's foreground window was nobody (or
the desktop) as the click arrived -- the frame was not "in front", and its
button brought it forward again instead of minimizing it (QA VM: the
foreground probe showed the frame gone for one 100 ms sample at the click).

The taskbar now remembers the last program window in front (not the bar,
the desktop or a passing surface, from EVENT_SYSTEM_FOREGROUND): a button
whose window is that one, while nothing else is in front, minimizes it.

Test: QA VM (the session's compositor; Xvfb keeps the focus): an xterm,
clicked into, then its button -- minimized (-32000), again -- restored;
before, the button left it in place. Mutant SG_MUTANT_BUTTON_FG_ONLY.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1808,12 +1808,42 @@
     sg_restore_hidden = 0;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: the last program window in front (not the bar, the
+ * desktop, a passing surface). A click on the taskbar takes the focus from
+ * a Linux program's window inside its frame for a moment (the X focus was
+ * the program's): Wine's foreground was nobody, or the desktop, as the click
+ * arrived, and the frame's button brought it forward again instead of
+ * minimizing it (David 2026-10-03). */
+static HWND sg_app_foreground;
+
+static BOOL sg_is_app_window( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    WCHAR class[64];
+    if (!hwnd || hwnd == tray_window || hwnd == GetDesktopWindow() || !IsWindowVisible( hwnd )) return FALSE;
+    if (sg_is_passing_surface( hwnd )) return FALSE;
+    return !(GetClassNameW( hwnd, class, ARRAY_SIZE(class) ) &&
+             (!wcscmp( class, L"Progman" ) || !wcscmp( class, L"WorkerW" ) || !wcscmp( class, L"Shell_TrayWnd" )));
+}
+
+/* hwnd is the window in front, for its taskbar button: it is the foreground
+ * window, or was the last program's window in front and nothing else is */
+static BOOL sg_button_window_in_front( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    HWND fg = GetForegroundWindow();
+    if (hwnd == fg) return TRUE;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_BUTTON_FG_ONLY
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
+    return hwnd == sg_app_foreground && !sg_is_app_window( fg );
+}
+
 /* a window brought forward, in any process (this one's File Explorer too) */
 static void CALLBACK sg_foreground_event( HWINEVENTHOOK hook, DWORD event, HWND hwnd, LONG object,
                                           LONG child, DWORD thread, DWORD time )
 {
     WCHAR class[64];
 
+    if (hwnd && object == OBJID_WINDOW && sg_is_app_window( hwnd )) sg_app_foreground = hwnd;
     if (!hwnd || object != OBJID_WINDOW) return;
     /* another window than the passing one came forward: it stays in front */
     if (sg_restore_popup && hwnd != sg_restore_popup && hwnd != GetDesktopWindow() && hwnd != tray_window &&
@@ -3076,7 +3106,7 @@
 
     if (IsWindowEnabled( hwnd ))
     {
-        if (hwnd == GetForegroundWindow())
+        if (sg_button_window_in_front( hwnd ))
         {
             SendMessageW( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_MINIMIZE, 0 );
             return;
